{"org":"elastic","repo":"elasticsearch","prNumber":"114334","commit":"fb2545dc8527e9a4805df779074b10460c0c9eab","generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"Max uses `field().dataType().noText()`, but Min, Top, and Values each inline the same logic as `DataType t \u003d field().dataType(); return t \u003d\u003d TEXT ? KEYWORD : t;`. Since `noText()` was introduced in this very PR to encapsulate exactly this rule, the three inline copies are redundant and will diverge if the TEXT→KEYWORD policy ever needs to change (e.g., to also handle `SEMANTIC_TEXT`). For consistency and a single source of truth, all four should use `noText()`.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Max.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Max.java-4583:4601-4575:4602","promptId":"#JE5T7","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Max.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Max.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":4583,"endPos":4601,"startLine":110,"startLineOffset":15,"endLine":110,"endLineOffset":33,"length":19}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":4575,"endPos":4602,"startLine":110,"startLineOffset":15,"endLine":110,"endLineOffset":42,"length":28}]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Values.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Values.java-4041:4059-4165:4197,4213:4236","promptId":"#3XA9T","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Values.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Values.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":4041,"endPos":4059,"startLine":94,"startLineOffset":15,"endLine":94,"endLineOffset":33,"length":19}],"dstChanges":[